<a2ui>
present_data takes an A2UI page as a JSON object (a JSON string is also accepted):

  {"title": "...", "components": [ {"id": "c1", "type": "...", ...}, ... ]}

Components form a flat list; nesting is by reference — a child sets
"parent" to its parent's id. Every component needs a unique "id".

Types and their fields (optional unless marked required):
  heading      text(required), level(1|2|3)
  text         text(required), muted
  divider      —
  callout      text(required), color, icon
  badge        text(required), color
  list         items(required, string[]), color, label
  code         text(required), language
  container    gap, layout(row|column|grid)
  statRow      —
  stat         label(required), color, connection, detail, sql, value
  table        columns(string[]), connection, label, rows(array of cell arrays), sql
  barChart     bars([{label, value}]), color, connection, label, motion({easing, speed, stagger, stiffness, damping, mass}), sql
  lineChart    color, connection, label, motion({easing, speed, stagger, stiffness, damping, mass}), points([{label, value}]), sql
  areaChart    columns(string[]), connection, label, motion({easing, speed, stagger, stiffness, damping, mass}), rows(array of cell arrays), sql
  columnChart  columns(string[]), connection, label, mode(stacked|grouped), motion({easing, speed, stagger, stiffness, damping, mass}), rows(array of cell arrays), sorted, sql
  ringChart    columns(string[]), connection, label, max(number > 0), motion({easing, speed, stagger, stiffness, damping, mass}), rows(array of cell arrays), sql
  radarChart   columns(string[]), connection, label, max(number > 0), motion({easing, speed, stagger, stiffness, damping, mass}), rows(array of cell arrays), sql
  sankeyChart  columns(string[]), connection, label, motion({easing, speed, stagger, stiffness, damping, mass}), rows(array of cell arrays), sql
  heatmap      columns(string[]), connection, label, motion({easing, speed, stagger, stiffness, damping, mass}), rows(array of cell arrays), sql
  streamChart  color, columns(string[]), connection, label, motion({easing, speed, stagger, stiffness, damping, mass}), refresh(number 5-3600), rows(array of cell arrays), sql, threshold, window(number 5-120)

color must be one of: "yellow", "black", "error", "muted".

Data binding: stat, table, barChart, lineChart, areaChart, ringChart, columnChart, radarChart, sankeyChart, heatmap, streamChart accept either inline data or
a "sql" field. "sql" bindings are READ-ONLY queries over this workspace's
connections — no INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/DDL/multiple statements in ANY sandbox mode
(the query re-runs on every render, so a write would fire each time); files only
by a literal absolute path inside data/, as for run_query. Prefer inline data in present_data: you
already have the values and the reply is a one-off, so there is nothing for a
live query to buy you.

A data-bound component may also set "connection" (a connection name, as accepted by
introspect_schema) to run its "sql" with that connection as the default for
unqualified table names; omit it for the workspace default.

SQL result shape: barChart and lineChart want a label column then a numeric
column (SELECT school, AVG(score) ...). stat wants a single number in the first
column of the first row. table renders whatever columns come back.
The other charts take inline "columns" + "rows" in exactly the shape their
sql returns:
  areaChart, columnChart, radarChart: a label column, then one numeric column per
    series (SELECT month, revenue, cost ...); columnChart mode stacked|grouped.
  ringChart: label, value[, max] per ring (max defaults to the "max" field, else 100).
  sankeyChart: source, target, weight per flow.
  heatmap: row label, column label, value per cell (SELECT node, hour, load ...).
  streamChart: label, value in time order; "refresh" (seconds) re-runs its sql
    while visible and keeps the last "window" points; values above "threshold" flag.

Every chart (barChart, lineChart, areaChart, ringChart, columnChart, radarChart, sankeyChart, heatmap, streamChart) animates in; "motion" tunes it:
easing one of "spring", "expo", "cinema", "steps", "custom", "none" ("custom" uses stiffness/damping/mass),
speed 0.25-4, stagger true|false. Omit motion for the default spring.

Do not add a heading component that just repeats the page's own "title" — the
title already renders above the components, so a duplicate heading is redundant
and, in the narrow panel this renders in, competes with it for space.
</a2ui>